      "_id": "0",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Let's look at this equation: 5 times the quantity x minus 3, equals 2x plus 9. We need to find x.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t001",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:00:00.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:00:50.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "1",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So we have 5(x - 3) = 2x + 9, and we're solving for x.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t002",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:00:52.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:20.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "2",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, that's the equation we're working with — got it clearly in mind now.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t003",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:27.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:53.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "3",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Okay, so... what should we do first with that parenthesis?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t004",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:00.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:21.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "4",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good question — think about what we need to do before we can combine like terms.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t005",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:22.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:37.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "5",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "We probably need to distribute the 5 into the parentheses first.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t006",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:37.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:58.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "6",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right. And after that, what's our goal with the x terms?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t007",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:03:04.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:04:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "7",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "We want to get all the x's on one side, so I'd move the 2x over.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t008",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:04:16.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:05:24.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "8",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Exactly — then once the x terms are together, what's left to do?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t009",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:05:27.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:05:41.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "9",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Then we just divide to get x by itself.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t010",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:05:42.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:13.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "10",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's the plan: expand, collect the x terms, then isolate x. Let's put it into action.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t011",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:21.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:36.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "11",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Alright, let me expand the left side: 5 times x is 5x, and 5 times -3 is -15.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t012",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:40.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:08.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "12",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good — so now the equation reads 5x - 15 = 2x + 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t013",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:14.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:33.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "13",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Now I'll subtract 2x from both sides: 5x minus 2x is 3x, so 3x - 15 = 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t014",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:41.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:08:46.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "14",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Nice. Now add 15 to both sides to get the x term alone.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t015",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:08:48.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:09:52.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "15",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 16,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "That gives 3x = 24.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t016",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:09:57.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:10:55.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "16",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 17,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "And now it's just one more move to finish — divide both sides by 3.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t017",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:10:55.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:11:33.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "17",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 18,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Wait, would it work if I moved the 2x first instead of subtracting it at that stage?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t018",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:11:40.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:16.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "18",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 19,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Sure, try it that way and see where it leads.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t019",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:22.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:13:26.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "19",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 20,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So starting from 5x - 15 = 2x + 9, I'd subtract 5x from both sides instead: -15 = -3x + 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t020",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:13:26.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "20",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 21,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Okay, keep going and see if you land on the same value for x.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t021",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:19.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:52.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "21",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s04",
      "sequence_id": 22,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Subtracting 9 gives -24 = -3x, and dividing by -3 gives x = 8 — same answer either way.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s04-t022",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:54.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:15:50.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "22",
